From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Cell borders: chunks built in the background, levelled
 creatures preloaded, unloading spread over frames

Crossing an exterior cell border did all its work in one frame. Each part is its own [Cells]
setting, read through the support library (support/src/cellborders.cpp):

background object paging: ObjectPaging::getChunk, asked by a view (cull, the focus ray) for a
chunk not in the cache, builds it on the work queue when another chunk can be drawn meanwhile:
the one taken out of the cache when an object of a loading cell was blacklisted (kept as a
stand-in unless next to the player), or the chunk of the same place for the other side of the
active grid's edge. RenderingManager::update rebuilds the terrain views once they are in. A
chunk started before the refs it holds changed is not cached.

preload levelled creatures: CreatureLevList::getModelsToPreload lists the models the list can
spawn at the player's level, so the cell preloader loads them.

spread cell unloading: Scene::changeCellGrid marks itself (Alpha3::CellBorderChange); the
collision objects of the cells it unloads leave the collision world a few each frame
(PhysicsSystem::releaseRemovedObjects, cell unload budget ms), and their fog of war is saved one
cell a frame (LocalMap::saveDeferredFogOfWar). Any other unload, or a save written, first does
what waits.
---
